# Line endings
# ===========
#
# Most of this repository is edited on Windows and the working copy is CRLF,
# which is harmless for source that only ever runs through Node.
#
# These are not harmless. A shell script whose shebang ends `bash\r` fails on
# Linux with a message that names neither the file nor the carriage return,
# and a systemd unit with CRLF line endings is rejected the same way. Both run
# only on the server, so the breakage would appear exactly once, during a
# deployment, and nowhere before it.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer   text eol=lf
